 02_3	Continue the same rule. Each coefficient is the previous one divided by the next whole number. We get one, one, one half, one sixth, one twenty-fourth. Those denominators are factorials. As we add terms, watch the polynomial change on the same axes. These curves are partial sums, not yet the exact solution.
